 "understanding": {
  "purpose": "A reference spec of the orders table's columns — an engineering artifact read to answer 'what columns exist, what type, can it be null, what's the default, what does it mean'. It is consulted, not compared numerically; the reader jumps to a column name and then reads across that row.",
  "reading": "Top-to-bottom scan of the Column column (identifiers are the index), then a rightward read of that row's Type / Nullable / Default, with Comment read only when needed. Cross-row comparison of Type values is secondary but real (repeated BIGINT UNSIGNED, TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE).",
  "groups": [
   "Column + Type form the identity pair — always read together and must never be broken mid-token",
   "Nullable + Default form the constraint pair — both are short flag-like values, low information density, safe to keep narrow",
   "Comment is prose, a separate register, and can absorb wrapping at line breaks"
  ],
  "keep_intact": [
   "column identifiers (order_reference, total_amount_cents, cancelled_at) — snake_case split across lines is misread as two columns",
   "type tokens (BIGINT UNSIGNED, VARCHAR(32), TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE) — breaking at spaces is tolerable, breaking inside a word is not",
   "default literals (CURRENT_TIMESTAMP) — a single token, must not split",
   "Nullable YES/NO — 3 characters, never wrap"
  ],
  "may_wrap": [
   "Comment — free prose, wraps at word boundaries with no loss",
   "Type — may wrap between its words (TIMESTAMP / WITH TIME ZONE) if words stay whole",
   "Default — may wrap to two lines if the token itself stays intact"
